<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ahab of Israel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahab was king of Israel in the 9th century BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a>, reigning from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> roughly between 871 and 852 BCE. He married the Phoenician princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jezebel">Jezebel</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> condemns him for promoting the worship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baal">Baal</a>. Assyrian records show him fielding 2,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qarqar">Battle of Qarqar</a> in 853 BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesha-stele">Mesha Stele</a> records that Moab was subject to his dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahab.jpg" alt="Ahab" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahab_rex.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
